WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.020
A man is defined by his ambitions.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.980
Before the Iron Crown, all the young lord had was an iron will.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.900
Little known and unestablished, the lord held some power,

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.660
but he wanted a kingdom to match his pride.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.080
So with ambition alone, he raised an army and threw his entire might against the kingdom of Venn.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.080
Venn was not a desirable region, but even so, the lord  lost much to acquire it.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.120
He wrested this small throne from its previous ruler and became the king.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.540
This act left him enfeebled.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.500
He had sacrificed everything for this kingdom

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.300
and was discovering that ambition without wisdom is like a bird without wings.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.820
How could he hope to hold this kingdom?

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.260
Ambition had inspired his subjects to action, yes.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.040
But ambition alone cannot run a country, it cannot substitute the qualities a ruler needs.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.640
The king was short-sighted; he knew little, and his story likely would've ended here

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.920
But then, from the east, a powerful warrior came.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.240
A man wielding a bewitched sword so powerful, it was unknown whether he controlled the blade

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.660
or whether the blade controlled him.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.900
This man was Alonne.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.060
Sir Alonne stands apart from the other characters in our story.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.340
The others are defined by their wants and ambitions,

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.060
but Alonne has none to speak of.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.820
Thus, it's impossible to say why he came to this land,

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.160
or what he saw in the kingdom.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.100
Perhaps he thought he was destined for great things

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.420
or perhaps they became like brothers.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.980
Whatever his desires, Alonne decided to serve the short-sighted king.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.520
His wisdom was a light in the darkness

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.680
and the king was reborn as a powerful ruler.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.760
With wisdom and pride, Alonne and the king did a great many things.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.380
Their rule was defined by their strength and the kingdom was shaped by their union.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.120
The king's army was revolutionised under Alonne,

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.560
with the men mastering great bows and slender blades, wielded in an eastern fashion.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:09.300
The king, as many kings before him, found himself enraptured with fire and all it represented.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:13.180
He appointed a master of pyromancy, a man named Eygil,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.240
who would go on to grant fire a will of its own.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:22.200
Eygil adored his bald-headed king and was awarded a great ornamental minotaur helm.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.460
The minotaur, half man, half bull, would come to symbolise

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.480
the stubbornness and beastial strength of the king and his kingdom.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.420
For even with Alonne's counsel, the king remained short-sighted and reckless.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.080
So, like a bull, he charged ahead, savouring his momentum.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.160
To sustain his country, the king sacrificed the land.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.660
Past the hunting grounds in the Copse, lay a place called 'Harvest Valley'.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.720
The king exploited the land here so thoroughly that poison seeped from the earth,

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.100
but it mattered not.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.480
The stubborn king persisted, adapting his workers and driving the slaves ever-harder.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.680
The bounty of ore found here was high,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.960
so the kingdom became wealthy and well-supplied.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.740
Within the valley, great relics of times long past were uncovered.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.640
Kingdoms from long ago, sunken and forgotten to time.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.800
A warning existed here, but the king was blind to it.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.020
He did not seek to learn from past kingdoms, buried beneath the earth.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.600
Rather, he intended to profit from their passing.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.820
And so when the scorching iron scepter was found, everything changed.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.520
With heat, you can fuel, create, destroy; it's one of the simplest forms of energy

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.560
and thus it's one of the most useful.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.560
With this artefact, the King of Venn revolutionised his kingdom.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.800
Smelting iron became trivial, there were no bounds to what he could create.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.520
Iron melted, shifted and was brought under his control,

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.120
as if he held sway over the forces of life and creation.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.420
The kingdom's warrior's were equipped in iron armament.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.360
Hulking great suits of armour were brought to life.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.160
The king curated a palace made entirely of iron.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:14.000
And some legends even say that he tried to create a dragon out of iron.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:18.140
Driven by the same-fated lunacy as the kings before him.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:23.180
Presiding over his great age, the Iron King knew unparalleled power;

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.160
none could stand in his way

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.240
and any who would try would be crushed under his might.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.460
Be that as it may, the Iron King still faced challenges.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:39.080
All the iron in the world could not cure the undead curse, but not for lack of trying on the king's part.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.780
He sought to shackle and imprison all undead in iron,

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.840
converting the Copse to a hunting ground and prison,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.840
where undead, not animals, were the prey.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.620
It seemed fruitless, however, and the hollowed undead continued to multiply

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.100
even within the ranks of those hunting them.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:02.120
In his rage, the Iron King built a great circular colosseum to torture the undead.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:07.280
They were ritually let out of their cells to be run down by the executioner chariot.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:14.120
Unable to escape and unable to die, the punishment for offending the Iron King's might was harsh,

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.900
even if undeserved.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.100
These things became reflections of the king's conceit; hallmarks of his reign.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:27.880
At this moment, a terrible women, who would be his ruinous queen, set course for the kingdom.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:33.380
And then, at the peak of the Iron Kingdom's rule, his friend walked away.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.980
Alonne was gone; his distaste left unspoken.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.600
The king was alone.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.220
How had Alonne dared to leave him?

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:46.520
The king's might was iron, his right to rule unchallenged.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.900
He could not suffer the indignity.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:49.760
Would not.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.000
So he tracked his old friend to a far-off keep.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:56.600
He saw that Alonne had brought some of the king's own men with him

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.160
and had posted them as guards, knowing the king would come after him.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.820
But the Iron King had grown powerful

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.420
and Alonne's knights were no match for his might.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.280
At the top of the tower, Alonne waited for his king to meet him.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.080
Once, the question the king might've asked was, "Why?"

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.900
"Why had Alonne left him?"

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.280
But he had been king for a long time and his arrogance had grown.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.960
So when the two men clashed, their ties were forgotten.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:28.340
They had come far together, ever since the days when the Iron King was just a small lord,

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.580
on a small throne.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.420
Alonne had helped him become the man he was today

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.140
and he paid dearly for it.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.320
For, once Alonne would've avoided every blow,

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:40.560
but now it was the king who overwhelmed the teacher.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.360
Alonne took his own life in the end,

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.060
dying with honour instead of to the king's hand.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:56.160
The memory we experience doesn't end with Alonne's death, as you would expect.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.120
When we step inside a memory, we see it through to the end.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.580
The king walked into the adjacent room after a long departed

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.740
and what he saw there would steal this memory in his mind forever.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.260
In this room, Alonne had kept the king's old throne,

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.240
a reminder of the king's humble origins.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.800
The keepsake from the time, he had travelled to the king's land,

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:27.220
offering his servitude and friendship to the man who would become the Iron King.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.780
The memory ends here.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:34.720
Nurtured properly, man's ambition allows us to take flight.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.920
On ambition's back, we reach greater heights

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.960
and kingdoms are elevated alongside the man.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.720
But if man looks back and sees not where he has been, then on which path does he travel?

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.500
The Iron King had lost his way

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.620
and now he had lost a friend and mentor as well.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:57.900
From this point onwards, we see evidence that this event had broken the man.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:03.560
After a long departed, the Iron King named his knights after Sir Alonne,

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.880
for they were loyal to him, more than the Iron King.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.540
He took Alonne's armour back to his home,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.500
enshrining it and locking it below his current towering, iron throne.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:20.220
This bonfire, below the throne, came to be known as 'Smelter Throne Bonfire'.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:25.440
His pyromancer, Eygil, had experimented with giving fire a will of its own.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:30.280
And the king had become adept at infusing suits of iron with souls.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.960
Now, towards the end of his rule, he crafted one more:

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:40.300
a terrifying suit of black iron that would come to represent the demons he now held.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:43.460
It's implied he infused it with Alonne's soul,

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:47.680
for the demon he created took on the combat style of his old friend,

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.600
battling with inhuman leaps into the air and the ability to infuse its sword with fire,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.900
by plunging it into his belly, just like Alonne had done.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.060
The lore is unclear on what happens next.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.840
Some of it says that the earth spouted fire, with a smelter demon arising from the flames.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:11.040
It says the short-sighted king was incinerated by the creature in one swing

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:14.140
and his castle devoured in a sea of flames.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.200
The other side of the lore says that the king hurled himself into the magma,

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.240
perhaps in agony over what he had done to his friend.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:29.640
Though, in the end, the queen of ruin arrives at the kingdom and finds no king or country.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:36.080
The short-sighted king had sunk below the scorching iron and his iron rule sunk with him.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.160
